      "answer": "Managed vector databases charge for the capacity that is kept running at all times\u2014often called \u201cpods.\u201d Because the service keeps the storage and compute resources available even when no queries are being executed, the monthly bill scales with the number of stored vectors regardless of query activity. This is why the cost grows even when nobody is querying the database. [1][2]",
